letely right but  it's actually even worse it's not just  20 Republicans in the Senate there is an  even smaller group that we could remove  Donald Trump because under the 25th  amendment just fourteen people could  remove a sitting president the 25th  amendment outlines a process for  removing a president who is either  unable or unfit  to serve section 4 of the 25th amendment  allows the vice president and a majority  of the cabinet to remove the president  from office under that fourth section it  would take 14 people to remove Donald  Trump vice president Mike Pence and 13  of the 24 cabinet members section 4  reads will put it up on the screen  whenever the vice president and a  majority of either the principal  officers of the executive departments or  of such other body as Congress may by  law provide transmit to the president  pro tempore of the Senate and the  Speaker of the House of Representatives  their written declaration that the  president is unable to discharge the  powers and duties of his office  the vice president shall immediately  assumed the powers and duties of the  office as acting president this is a  very quick and simple process in a sense  consider the immorality of being able to  end this national nightmare among a  group of just 20 Republicans in the  Senate among a group of 14 Republicans  in the cabinet including Mike Pence and  choosing not to do it this is the virus  of political partisanship and cronyism  that we've been talking about will I  talked earlier in the show we just need  for Republicans to say let's subpoena  john bolton for republicans in the  senate and then we can do it that gets  us a simple majority we will be  hard-pressed to find four Republican  senators who are willing just to do the  very milquetoast uncontroversial thing  of subpoenaing john bolton to testify in  Donald Trump's impeachment trial  forget about 14 Republicans in the  cabinet or 20 Republicans in the Senate  but my bet if I were to bet is they go  down with the ship or try to outlast  this there is ZERO indication that any  of these people want to be a part of the  solution or that they even really agree  about what the solution is good luck  finding 20 Republicans with a conscience  let alone Republican senators you would  have better luck getting a Santa the  Tooth Fairy and the Easter Bunny to  remove Donald Trump in  20 then you would finding 20 Republican  senators or 14 Republican cabinet  members to make it a reality we're going  to have to do it without them and I can  you know it when I said this a year and  a half ago it felt like maybe it wasn't  the case a year and a half ago I was  saying Trump clearly should be impeached  Trump clearly should be removed under  the 25th amendment something seems  cognitively wrong something is very  wrong in terms of the degree of  corruption that this guy is  participating in but a year and a half  ago I was saying I still believe the  Moller report isn't going to do it  impeachment isn't going to do it  November of 2020 is very quickly going  to become the first soonest and best  opportunity to remove the guy we're now  only just under you know 10 10 months -  a week away from the November of 2020  election it is becoming clearer and  clearer that that is the quickest most  efficient and most direct way to remove  the guy I hope we recognize that I hope  we don't allow the activism that so many  people have participated in since Donald  Trump was first elected to kind of fade  and the enthusiasm to wane we've got to  remember the opportunity is coming up  it's less than 10 months away
 

